// ThreadConstantBranches — a Std→Std pass that decides a join block's branch at the EDGES that already
// know the answer.
//
// THE SHAPE. A block C with block args whose whole body is one `cmpImm` of one of its own block args
// (slot k) against an immediate, and whose terminator is a `condBranch` on that compare. When a
// predecessor passes a `const` for slot k, the test's answer is fixed the moment that edge is taken.
//
// THE REWRITE keeps C as the join, so no phi is rebuilt anywhere:
//   • every constant-passing predecessor must decide the SAME target X. C's terminator becomes
//     `branch(X)`, and C loses the compare, its edge to the other target Y, and block-arg slot k;
//   • every other predecessor P gets the compare on its own incoming value for slot k and a `condBranch`
//     between Y and C, keeping C's then/else orientation, plus an edge to Y — C's edge args with C's own
//     block args replaced by P's incoming values by slot — when Y takes block args.
// A C left holding only `branch(X)` is removed by the Target-tier jump threading (`BranchCleanup`), so
// a constant-passing predecessor reaches X with no test, no copy of the constant and no jump.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS. Every `try f(…) otherwise …` whose callee `inlineManagedPrimitives` expanded ends in a
// continuation `__im_cont(value, flag)`: the fast arm passes `const 0` for the flag, the slow arm the
// call's real flag, and the continuation's body is the `try`'s own `flag != 0` test. The fast path —
// every checked element read and write — paid a constant, a phi copy, a compare and a branch for an
// answer known where the edge is. The rule is stated for any phi of constants feeding a branch.
//
// THE RULE, clause by clause:
//   • The compare's result is read only by C's terminator, and the tested arg only by the compare. The
//     `otherwise (e)` binding forms and a rethrowing bare `try` read the flag in `tryerr`, which the
//     rewrite reaches from P directly, where C's block args are not defined.
//   • Every predecessor reaches C through `branch(C)` with exactly that one edge. A `condBranch` or
//     `switch` predecessor would need one arm retargeted, which is a different rewrite, and a physical
//     fall-through has no terminator op to overwrite.
//   • The constant-deciding predecessors agree on X, and there is at least one. Two answers would need
//     two exits from C.
//   • X has exactly one predecessor, C. That is what keeps X dominated by C once P's edges to Y exist:
//     every block X dominates keeps X as a dominator (a new path P→Y→…→B avoiding X would have been the
//     old path P→C→Y→…→B, which also avoided X), so C's block args stay defined wherever they are read.
//   • Every read of C's other block args is in a block X dominates, or is an arg on one of C's own edges:
//     the edge to X keeps C's definitions in scope, and the edge to Y is what the P→Y edges are built from.
//   • An unsigned compare is declined by the evaluator this pass shares with `foldConstants`.
// A constant that reaches C THROUGH an empty forwarding join — an `else if` chain's inner merge, left
// with one predecessor once `foldConstants` folded the outer `if` — is not seen: the value C's
// predecessor passes is that join's block arg, and `elimTrivialBlockArgs` has already run.
//
// SCHEDULING: right after `foldConstOperands`, which is what makes the test a `cmpImm`.
//
// EVERY CANDIDATE IS CHECKED ON THE FUNCTION BEFORE ANY REWRITE, AND THE REWRITES ARE APPLIED TOGETHER.
// That is sound because two admitted candidates are never adjacent: a candidate's successors are
// reached through its `condBranch`, which refuses the successor as a candidate. So one rewrite changes
// the terminators of blocks that are no other candidate's predecessor (its own P's, which end in a
// `branch` to it, and itself), adds edges only into its Y, which is no candidate, and mints reads only of
// values already read in the same block — P's incoming value, and C's own edge args to Y.
//
// A REWRITE CAN ORPHAN A REGION: a C with no non-constant predecessor leaves its Y with no way in, and
// everything only Y reached goes with it — possibly another admitted candidate, already rewritten and
// counted. So the tested slots are dropped FIRST, while every rewritten join is still registered and
// the count can be checked, and the unreachable region is removed after that. A Y whose only remaining
// way in is itself unreachable is the same allocator hazard, so the removal runs after every function
// that rewrote anything, not only where a Y visibly lost its last predecessor.

typealias ThreadedSiteCount = int(0 to u64.max)
typealias CandidateIndex = int(0 to u64.max)
typealias ArgSlot = int(0 to u64.max)

// Why the rule left a SHAPED block alone. Counted per reason into the pass summary and named in the
// per-site trace, so a reader can tell what widening the rule would buy before writing the widening.
enum ThreadRefusal
	unreachable
	conditionReadElsewhere
	testedArgReadElsewhere
	predecessorNotALoneBranch
	unsignedCompare
	targetsDisagree
	noConstantPredecessor
	keptTargetHasAnotherWayIn
	valueArgReadOutsideKeptTarget
end 'ThreadRefusal'

function refusalText(reason ThreadRefusal) returns String
	return match reason 'r'
		unreachable gives "the entry cannot reach it"
		conditionReadElsewhere gives "its compare's result is read by more than the terminator"
		testedArgReadElsewhere gives "the tested block arg is read by more than the compare"
		predecessorNotALoneBranch gives "a predecessor does not reach it through a lone `branch`"
		unsignedCompare gives "the compare is unsigned, which the shared evaluator declines"
		targetsDisagree gives "two constant predecessors decide different targets"
		noConstantPredecessor gives "no predecessor passes a constant for the tested arg"
		keptTargetHasAnotherWayIn gives "the target its constants decide has a predecessor other than the join"
		valueArgReadOutsideKeptTarget gives "another block arg is read in a block the kept target does not dominate"
	end 'r'
end 'refusalText'

// What every function's scan refills, created ONCE for the module: the candidate list (`Array.clear`
// keeps its capacity), the two classification records the scan reads ops into, and the refusal tally.
// Per function these would be three allocations paid by the many functions that hold no candidate.
type ThreadScratch
	export var candidates as ThreadCandidateArray
	export var arith as StdArithOperands
	export var branch as StdBranchOperands
	// One count per `ThreadRefusal`, for the whole module.
	export var refusals as OrdinalTally

	static function create() returns ThreadScratch
		return Self{candidates: ThreadCandidateArray.create(), arith: StdArithOperands.create(), branch: StdBranchOperands.create(), refusals: OrdinalTally.create(ThreadRefusal.allCases.count())}
	end 'create'
end 'ThreadScratch'

// Thread every admissible join block in every function, in place.
export function threadConstantBranches(project Project, module StdModule)
	var threaded = 0 as ThreadedSiteCount
	var scratch = ThreadScratch.create()

	// An INDEX loop, not `for … in`: the element is a BORROW of `module`, and the call below is
	// recorded as writing that same storage — canonical note at
	// `IR/Std/ElimTrivialBlockArgs.elimTrivialBlockArgs`.
	for fnIndex in 0 upto module.functions.count() 'eachFunc'
		threaded = threaded + threadConstantBranchesInFunc(module, func: try module.functions.get(fnIndex) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: fnIndex {fnIndex} is below module.functions.count()"), funcIndex: fnIndex, origins: project.valueOrigins, scratch: scratch)
	end 'eachFunc'

	let total = threaded
	logDebug(LogCategory.ir, message: function() gives "threadConstantBranches: threaded {total} site(s) across {module.funcCount()} function(s); shaped blocks left alone: {scratch.refusals.summary(ThreadRefusal.allCaseNames)}")
end 'threadConstantBranches'

// One join block that has the SHAPE, and — once `admit` has run — whether the rule admits it and
// which target it keeps. Positions are `func.blockRefs` positions, the key space `StdDominatorTree`
// answers in.
type ThreadCandidate
	export var position as BlockRefIndex
	export var blockRef as BlockRef
	export var blockId as BlockId
	export var compareOpIdx as OpIndex
	// The compare's result, read only by the terminator.
	export var condId as ValueId
	// The block arg the compare tests, and its slot.
	export var testedArg as ValueId
	export var testedSlot as ArgSlot
	export var imm as Imm32
	export var pred as StdCmpPred
	export var operandType as StdType
	export var thenBlockId as BlockId
	export var elseBlockId as BlockId
	export var admitted = false
	// Filled by `admit`: the target every constant-passing predecessor decides (X), its position, and
	// the other target (Y).
	export var keptTarget as BlockId = 0
	export var keptPosition as BlockRefIndex = 0
	export var droppedTarget as BlockId = 0

	static function create(position BlockRefIndex, blockRef BlockRef, blockId BlockId, compareOpIdx OpIndex, condId ValueId, testedArg ValueId, testedSlot ArgSlot, imm Imm32, pred StdCmpPred, operandType StdType, thenBlockId BlockId, elseBlockId BlockId) returns ThreadCandidate
		return Self{position: position, blockRef: blockRef, blockId: blockId, compareOpIdx: compareOpIdx, condId: condId, testedArg: testedArg, testedSlot: testedSlot, imm: imm, pred: pred, operandType: operandType, thenBlockId: thenBlockId, elseBlockId: elseBlockId}
	end 'create'
end 'ThreadCandidate'

typealias ThreadCandidateArray = Array with ThreadCandidate

// Thread one function. Returns how many join blocks it rewrote.
function threadConstantBranchesInFunc(module StdModule, func IrFunction, funcIndex FuncIndex, origins ValueOriginTable, scratch ThreadScratch) returns ThreadedSiteCount
	collectThreadCandidates(module, func: func, scratch: scratch)
	if scratch.candidates.count() == 0 'noCandidate'
		// The common case, and the only cost most functions pay: one op read per block.
		return 0
	end 'noCandidate'

	let analysis = FunctionAnalysis.gather(module, func: func, scratch: scratch)
	let bound = blockArgIdBound(module, func: func)
	var argOwner = ValueIdArray.create()
	argOwner.resize(bound)
	var argSlot = ValueIdArray.create()
	argSlot.resize(bound)

	var admittedCount = 0 as ThreadedSiteCount
	for index in 0 upto scratch.candidates.count() 'eachCandidate'
		var candidate = try scratch.candidates.get(index) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: candidates.get OOB at {index}")
		if admit(module, func: func, analysis: analysis, candidate: candidate) 'admitted'
			candidate.admitted = true
			admittedCount = admittedCount + 1
			recordBlockArgOwner(module, candidate: candidate, index: index, argOwner: argOwner, argSlot: argSlot)
		end 'admitted'
	end 'eachCandidate'

	if admittedCount == 0 'nothingAdmitted'
		return 0
	end 'nothingAdmitted'

	refuseEscapingReads(module, func: func, analysis: analysis, candidates: scratch.candidates, argOwner: argOwner)

	return applyAdmitted(module, func: func, funcIndex: funcIndex, origins: origins, analysis: analysis, candidates: scratch.candidates, argOwner: argOwner, argSlot: argSlot)
end 'threadConstantBranchesInFunc'

// Every block with the SHAPE — block args, exactly one body op which is a `cmpImm` on one of them, and
// a `condBranch` on that compare between two distinct targets — into `scratch.candidates`. Whether the
// rule ADMITS a block is `admit`'s question, asked only of a function that has at least one of these.
function collectThreadCandidates(module StdModule, func IrFunction, scratch ThreadScratch)
	scratch.candidates.clear()

	for position in 0 upto func.blockRefs.count() 'eachBlock'
		let blockRef = try func.blockRefs.get(position) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: blockRefs.get OOB at {position}")
		let block = module.getBlock(blockRef)

		if block.blockArgs.count() == 0 or block.opRefs.count() != 1 or not block.hasTerminatorOp() 'notTheShape'
			continue
		end 'notTheShape'

		let compareOpIdx = try block.opRefs.get(0) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: opRefs.get(0) on a one-op block")
		classifyArithOperands(module.getOp(compareOpIdx), operands: scratch.arith)
		if not scratch.arith.isComparisonImm() 'notACompare'
			continue
		end 'notACompare'

		classifyBranch(module.getOp(block.terminatorIndex()), out: scratch.branch)
		if not scratch.branch.isCondBranch() 'notACondBranch'
			continue
		end 'notACondBranch'

		pushIfBranchOnTheCompare(scratch.candidates, block: block, position: position, blockRef: blockRef, compareOpIdx: compareOpIdx, operands: scratch.arith, condId: scratch.branch.condId, thenBlockId: scratch.branch.thenBlockId, elseBlockId: scratch.branch.elseBlockId)
	end 'eachBlock'
end 'collectThreadCandidates'

// The last two shape questions, asked once the terminator is known to be a `condBranch`: it must test
// THIS compare, the compare must read one of the block's own args, and the two arms must differ (one
// arm named twice has two edges to tell apart — the case `foldConstants.foldCondBranch` refuses too).
function pushIfBranchOnTheCompare(candidates ThreadCandidateArray, block IrBlock, position BlockRefIndex, blockRef BlockRef, compareOpIdx OpIndex, operands StdArithOperands, condId ValueId, thenBlockId BlockId, elseBlockId BlockId)
	if condId != operands.resultId or thenBlockId == elseBlockId 'notTheShape'
		return
	end 'notTheShape'

	for slot in 0 upto block.blockArgs.count() 'eachArg'
		let arg = try block.blockArgs.get(slot) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: blockArgs.get OOB at {slot}")
		if arg.valueId == operands.lhs 'testsThisArg'
			candidates.push(ThreadCandidate.create(position, blockRef: blockRef, blockId: block.id, compareOpIdx: compareOpIdx, condId: condId, testedArg: operands.lhs, testedSlot: slot, imm: operands.imm, pred: operands.pred, operandType: operands.operandType, thenBlockId: thenBlockId, elseBlockId: elseBlockId))
			return
		end 'testsThisArg'
	end 'eachArg'
end 'pushIfBranchOnTheCompare'

// The per-function facts every admission question reads, gathered ONCE for a function that has at
// least one candidate: the constants, the dominator tree with O(1) dominance stamps, the function-wide
// use multiplicities, and the block-id → position index.
type FunctionAnalysis
	export var constMap as ConstValueMap
	export var tree as StdDominatorTree
	export var stamps as DominatorStamps
	export var valueUses as StdValueUseSet
	export var positionById as BlockIndexById
	// The pass's refusal tally and terminator record, aliased in from `ThreadScratch`: every clause
	// that refuses, and every predecessor read, already holds this record.
	export var refusals as OrdinalTally
	export var branch as StdBranchOperands

	static function gather(module StdModule, func IrFunction, scratch ThreadScratch) returns FunctionAnalysis
		var def = StdFoldableDef.create()
		let constMap = collectConstValues(module, opIndices: module.liveOpIndices(func), def: def)
		let tree = StdDominatorTree.build(module, func: func)
		var valueUses = StdValueUseSet.createTrackingRepeats()
		collectFunctionValueUses(module, func: func, referenced: valueUses)
		return Self{constMap: constMap, tree: tree, stamps: DominatorStamps.build(tree), valueUses: valueUses, positionById: module.blockIndexById(func), refusals: scratch.refusals, branch: scratch.branch}
	end 'gather'

	function positionOf(blockId BlockId) returns BlockRefIndex
		return try self.positionById.get(blockId) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: block {blockId} is a branch target of this function but is not in its blockRefs")
	end 'positionOf'
end 'FunctionAnalysis'

// The rule's clauses about the candidate itself and its neighbours — everything but the reads of its
// other block args, which `refuseEscapingReads` checks for every admitted candidate in one walk.
function admit(module StdModule, func IrFunction, analysis FunctionAnalysis, candidate ThreadCandidate) returns bool
	if not analysis.tree.canReach(candidate.position) 'unreachable'
		return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.unreachable, analysis: analysis)
	end 'unreachable'

	if analysis.valueUses.containsRepeat(candidate.condId) 'conditionReadElsewhere'
		return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.conditionReadElsewhere, analysis: analysis)
	end 'conditionReadElsewhere'

	if analysis.valueUses.containsRepeat(candidate.testedArg) 'testedArgReadElsewhere'
		return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.testedArgReadElsewhere, analysis: analysis)
	end 'testedArgReadElsewhere'

	if not decideTargetFromPredecessors(module, func: func, analysis: analysis, candidate: candidate) 'predecessorsRefuse'
		return false
	end 'predecessorsRefuse'

	// "X has one predecessor" implies "C dominates X" only for a non-entry X: the entry has no predecessor
	// at all and dominates everything, so it is refused before the degree is read.
	candidate.keptPosition = analysis.positionOf(candidate.keptTarget)
	if candidate.keptPosition == StdEntryBlockPosition or analysis.tree.pred.degree(candidate.keptPosition as CsrIndex) != 1 'keptTargetHasAnotherWayIn'
		return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.keptTargetHasAnotherWayIn, analysis: analysis)
	end 'keptTargetHasAnotherWayIn'

	return true
end 'admit'

// Count and trace one refusal. Answers `false` so a clause can `return refuse(…)`.
function refuse(candidate ThreadCandidate, reason ThreadRefusal, analysis FunctionAnalysis) returns bool
	analysis.refusals.add(reason.ordinal, count: 1)
	logTrace(LogCategory.ir, message: function() gives "threadConstantBranches: block_{candidate.blockId} left alone — {refusalText(reason)}")
	return false
end 'refuse'

// Walk C's predecessors: each must reach C through `branch(C)` with that one edge; each that passes a
// constant in the tested slot must decide the same target. Writes `keptTarget`/`droppedTarget` and
// answers whether at least one constant predecessor decided.
function decideTargetFromPredecessors(module StdModule, func IrFunction, analysis FunctionAnalysis, candidate ThreadCandidate) returns bool
	var decided = false
	let join = module.getBlock(candidate.blockRef)

	for k in 0 upto analysis.tree.pred.degree(candidate.position as CsrIndex) 'eachPred'
		let predPosition = analysis.tree.pred.neighbour(candidate.position as CsrIndex, k: k) as BlockRefIndex
		let pred = module.blockAtPosition(func, position: predPosition)

		if not predecessorBranchesOnlyTo(module, pred: pred, targetId: candidate.blockId, branch: analysis.branch) 'notABranchPredecessor'
			return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.predecessorNotALoneBranch, analysis: analysis)
		end 'notABranchPredecessor'

		let incoming = incomingArgAt(soleEdge(pred), k: candidate.testedSlot as ValueId, pred: pred, target: join)
		if not analysis.constMap.contains(incoming) 'runtimeValue'
			continue
		end 'runtimeValue'

		var target = candidate.thenBlockId
		match evaluateIntCompare(candidate.pred, lhs: analysis.constMap.constantOf(incoming), rhs: candidate.imm as ParsedInt, operandType: candidate.operandType) 'verdict'
			folded(payload) then target = candidate.thenBlockId if payload != ConditionIsFalse else candidate.elseBlockId
			notFoldable then return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.unsignedCompare, analysis: analysis)
		end 'verdict'

		if decided and target != candidate.keptTarget 'twoAnswers'
			return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.targetsDisagree, analysis: analysis)
		end 'twoAnswers'

		decided = true
		candidate.keptTarget = target
		candidate.droppedTarget = candidate.elseBlockId if target == candidate.thenBlockId else candidate.thenBlockId
	end 'eachPred'

	if not decided 'noConstantPredecessor'
		return refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.noConstantPredecessor, analysis: analysis)
	end 'noConstantPredecessor'

	return true
end 'decideTargetFromPredecessors'

// Whether `pred` ends in `branch(targetId)` and carries exactly that one edge — the only predecessor
// shape whose terminator the rewrite can overwrite with a `condBranch`.
function predecessorBranchesOnlyTo(module StdModule, pred IrBlock, targetId BlockId, branch StdBranchOperands) returns bool
	if not pred.hasTerminatorOp() or pred.branchEdges.count() != 1 'notOneBranch'
		return false
	end 'notOneBranch'

	let edge = try pred.branchEdges.get(0) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: branchEdges.get(0) on a one-edge block")
	if edge.targetBlockId != targetId 'edgeElsewhere'
		return false
	end 'edgeElsewhere'

	classifyBranch(module.getOp(pred.terminatorIndex()), out: branch)
	return branch.isBranch() and branch.targetBlockId == targetId
end 'predecessorBranchesOnlyTo'

// The one edge `pred` carries. Read through a function so the borrow of `pred` ends at the return —
// the rewrite appends to the block while it still holds the edge's args.
function soleEdge(pred IrBlock) returns BranchEdge
	return try pred.branchEdges.get(0) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: branchEdges.get(0) on a one-edge block")
end 'soleEdge'

// Index C's block args by value id: which admitted candidate owns each (its index plus one, so the
// zero-filled column carries its own "no candidate" answer, as `buildBlockIdIndex` does) and at which
// slot. Both are what the read walk and the edge substitution look up per value, in O(1).
function recordBlockArgOwner(module StdModule, candidate ThreadCandidate, index CandidateIndex, argOwner ValueIdArray, argSlot ValueIdArray)
	let block = module.getBlock(candidate.blockRef)
	for slot in 0 upto block.blockArgs.count() 'eachArg'
		let arg = try block.blockArgs.get(slot) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: blockArgs.get OOB at {slot}")
		try argOwner.set(arg.valueId, value: index + 1) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: block arg {arg.valueId} is outside the block-arg id space")
		try argSlot.set(arg.valueId, value: slot) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: block arg {arg.valueId} is outside the block-arg id space")
	end 'eachArg'
end 'recordBlockArgOwner'

// The `argOwner` entry of a block arg no admitted candidate owns — the zero the column is filled with.
let UnownedBlockArg = 0 as ValueId

// Whether an admitted candidate owns block arg `valueId`. Ids above the block-arg space are op results
// and parameters, which no candidate owns. Two questions rather than one returned union, for
// `StdFoldableDef`'s measured reason: this is asked once per value READ in the function.
function isOwnedByACandidate(valueId ValueId, argOwner ValueIdArray) returns bool
	if valueId >= argOwner.count() 'notABlockArg'
		return false
	end 'notABlockArg'

	let ownerPlusOne = try argOwner.get(valueId) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: argOwner.get OOB at {valueId}")
	return ownerPlusOne != UnownedBlockArg
end 'isOwnedByACandidate'

// The candidate that owns block arg `valueId`. Panics for one no candidate owns — every caller has
// asked `isOwnedByACandidate` first, and no index answers for "none" that is not some candidate's.
function candidateOwning(valueId ValueId, argOwner ValueIdArray) returns CandidateIndex
	let ownerPlusOne = try argOwner.get(valueId) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: argOwner.get OOB at {valueId}")
	if ownerPlusOne == UnownedBlockArg 'unowned'
		panic("threadConstantBranches: block arg {valueId} is owned by no admitted candidate — ask `isOwnedByACandidate` first")
	end 'unowned'

	return (ownerPlusOne - 1) as CandidateIndex
end 'candidateOwning'

// The last clause of the rule, for every admitted candidate in ONE walk of the function's reads: a
// read of a candidate's block arg — other than the tested one, whose reads the repeat test settled —
// must sit in a block the kept target dominates, or be an arg on the candidate's own edges. Any other
// read refuses the candidate.
function refuseEscapingReads(module StdModule, func IrFunction, analysis FunctionAnalysis, candidates ThreadCandidateArray, argOwner ValueIdArray)
	var reads = StdValueUseSet.createRecordingIds()

	for position in 0 upto func.blockRefs.count() 'eachBlock'
		let block = module.blockAtPosition(func, position: position)

		for opIdx in block.opRefs 'eachOp'
			refuseEscapingOpReads(module, opIdx: opIdx, position: position, analysis: analysis, candidates: candidates, argOwner: argOwner, reads: reads)
		end 'eachOp'

		if block.hasTerminatorOp() 'hasTerm'
			refuseEscapingOpReads(module, opIdx: block.terminatorIndex(), position: position, analysis: analysis, candidates: candidates, argOwner: argOwner, reads: reads)
		end 'hasTerm'

		for edge in block.branchEdges 'eachEdge'
			for argId in edge.argIds 'eachArg'
				refuseIfReadEscapes(argId, position: position, isEdgeArg: true, analysis: analysis, candidates: candidates, argOwner: argOwner)
			end 'eachArg'
		end 'eachEdge'
	end 'eachBlock'
end 'refuseEscapingReads'

function refuseEscapingOpReads(module StdModule, opIdx OpIndex, position BlockRefIndex, analysis FunctionAnalysis, candidates ThreadCandidateArray, argOwner ValueIdArray, reads StdValueUseSet)
	reads.clear()
	collectStdOpUses(module.getOp(opIdx), referenced: reads)

	for i in 0 upto reads.insertedIdCount() 'eachRead'
		refuseIfReadEscapes(reads.insertedIdAt(i), position: position, isEdgeArg: false, analysis: analysis, candidates: candidates, argOwner: argOwner)
	end 'eachRead'
end 'refuseEscapingOpReads'

function refuseIfReadEscapes(valueId ValueId, position BlockRefIndex, isEdgeArg bool, analysis FunctionAnalysis, candidates ThreadCandidateArray, argOwner ValueIdArray)
	if not isOwnedByACandidate(valueId, argOwner: argOwner) 'unowned'
		return
	end 'unowned'

	let index = candidateOwning(valueId, argOwner: argOwner)
	refuseIfOwnedReadEscapes(try candidates.get(index) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: candidates.get OOB at {index}"), valueId: valueId, position: position, isEdgeArg: isEdgeArg, analysis: analysis)
end 'refuseIfReadEscapes'

function refuseIfOwnedReadEscapes(candidate ThreadCandidate, valueId ValueId, position BlockRefIndex, isEdgeArg bool, analysis FunctionAnalysis)
	if not candidate.admitted or valueId == candidate.testedArg 'nothingToCheck'
		return
	end 'nothingToCheck'

	if position == candidate.position 'readInTheJoinItself'
		if isEdgeArg 'onItsOwnEdge'
			return
		end 'onItsOwnEdge'

		panic("threadConstantBranches: block arg {valueId} of block_{candidate.blockId} is read by an op of its own block, whose only op is the compare on a different arg")
	end 'readInTheJoinItself'

	if not analysis.tree.canReach(position) or not analysis.stamps.dominates(candidate.keptPosition, b: position) 'escapes'
		candidate.admitted = refuse(candidate, reason: ThreadRefusal.valueArgReadOutsideKeptTarget, analysis: analysis)
	end 'escapes'
end 'refuseIfOwnedReadEscapes'

// Rewrite every admitted candidate, then the function-wide follow-ups the rewrites owe: the compares
// come out of their blocks, an orphaned Y comes out of the function, the tested slots come off their
// blocks and every incoming edge, and the constants nothing reads any more are retired.
function applyAdmitted(module StdModule, func IrFunction, funcIndex FuncIndex, origins ValueOriginTable, analysis FunctionAnalysis, candidates ThreadCandidateArray, argOwner ValueIdArray, argSlot ValueIdArray) returns ThreadedSiteCount
	// Seeded ONCE, before any rewrite, past every id the function uses; each duplicated compare mints
	// its result from here.
	var minter = ValueMinter.create(nextFreeValueId(module, func: func) as ParamCount)
	var doomedCompares = StdValueUseSet.create()
	var applied = 0 as ThreadedSiteCount

	for index in 0 upto candidates.count() 'eachCandidate'
		let candidate = try candidates.get(index) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: candidates.get OOB at {index}")
		if not candidate.admitted 'refused'
			continue
		end 'refused'

		threadOne(module, func: func, funcIndex: funcIndex, origins: origins, analysis: analysis, candidate: candidate, index: index, argOwner: argOwner, argSlot: argSlot, minter: minter)
		doomedCompares.insert(candidate.condId)
		applied = applied + 1
	end 'eachCandidate'

	if applied == 0 'nothingApplied'
		return 0
	end 'nothingApplied'

	removeOpsDefining(module, func: func, doomed: doomedCompares)

	// BEFORE the unreachable region goes: a rewritten join inside it must still be registered when its
	// slot is dropped and counted — see the header.
	dropTestedSlots(module, func: func, candidates: candidates, applied: applied)

	// A Y no reachable predecessor reaches any more may feed a phi from code no path runs, which is the
	// allocator hazard `dropUnreachableBlocks` states.
	dropUnreachableBlocks(module, func: func)

	// The `const`s the constant-passing predecessors fed into the dropped slots — retired by the same
	// narrow rule `foldConstOperands` owns, over the ops the rewrites left live.
	dceRetiredDefs(module, func: func, opIndices: module.liveOpIndices(func), def: StdFoldableDef.create())

	return applied
end 'applyAdmitted'

// The rewrite of one join block C and its predecessors. The tree's predecessor list is read AFTER
// earlier rewrites in the same function and is still exact — see the header for why no rewrite
// changes an admitted candidate's predecessors.
function threadOne(module StdModule, func IrFunction, funcIndex FuncIndex, origins ValueOriginTable, analysis FunctionAnalysis, candidate ThreadCandidate, index CandidateIndex, argOwner ValueIdArray, argSlot ValueIdArray, minter ValueMinter)
	var join = module.getBlock(candidate.blockRef)
	let dropped = module.blockAtPosition(func, position: analysis.positionOf(candidate.droppedTarget))
	let droppedTakesArgs = dropped.blockArgs.count() != 0
	let argsToDropped = edgeArgsTo(join, targetId: candidate.droppedTarget, takesArgs: droppedTakesArgs)

	for k in 0 upto analysis.tree.pred.degree(candidate.position as CsrIndex) 'eachPred'
		let predPosition = analysis.tree.pred.neighbour(candidate.position as CsrIndex, k: k) as BlockRefIndex
		var pred = module.blockAtPosition(func, position: predPosition)
		let incoming = incomingArgAt(soleEdge(pred), k: candidate.testedSlot as ValueId, pred: pred, target: join)

		if analysis.constMap.contains(incoming) 'decidedAtTheEdge'
			continue
		end 'decidedAtTheEdge'

		duplicateTestInto(module, pred: pred, candidate: candidate, index: index, incoming: incoming, argsToDropped: argsToDropped, droppedTakesArgs: droppedTakesArgs, argOwner: argOwner, argSlot: argSlot, funcIndex: funcIndex, origins: origins, minter: minter)
	end 'eachPred'

	// In place at its own index — `setTerminator` appends and would orphan the old op.
	try module.ops.set(join.terminatorIndex(), value: StdOp.branch(candidate.keptTarget)) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: ops.set OOB at terminator index {join.terminatorIndex()}")
	join.branchEdges = edgesWithoutTarget(join.branchEdges, droppedTarget: candidate.droppedTarget)

	logTrace(LogCategory.ir, message: function() gives "threadConstantBranches: block_{candidate.blockId} branches to block_{candidate.keptTarget} unconditionally; block_{candidate.droppedTarget} is reached from the non-constant predecessors directly")
end 'threadOne'

// The args C's edge to `targetId` carries. A target that takes block args MUST have an edge (the
// phi model records one edge per successor that carries phis); one that takes none has none.
module function edgeArgsTo(join IrBlock, targetId BlockId, takesArgs bool) returns ValueIdArray
	for edge in join.branchEdges 'eachEdge'
		if edge.targetBlockId == targetId 'found'
			return edge.argIds
		end 'found'
	end 'eachEdge'

	if takesArgs 'missingEdge'
		panic("threadConstantBranches: block_{join.id} branches to block_{targetId}, which takes block args, but carries no edge to it")
	end 'missingEdge'

	return ValueIdArray.create()
end 'edgeArgsTo'

// Give one non-constant predecessor P the test: the compare on its own incoming value, a `condBranch`
// in C's then/else orientation with the dropped target's arm pointing there and the other arm at C, and
// a fresh edge column — the edge to C it had, plus the edge to the dropped target when that takes args.
function duplicateTestInto(module StdModule, pred IrBlock, candidate ThreadCandidate, index CandidateIndex, incoming ValueId, argsToDropped ValueIdArray, droppedTakesArgs bool, argOwner ValueIdArray, argSlot ValueIdArray, funcIndex FuncIndex, origins ValueOriginTable, minter ValueMinter)
	var predBlock = pred
	let argsToJoin = soleEdge(predBlock).argIds

	// The duplicated test answers to the statement the original compare did, and stands in for its result.
	module.spans.current = module.spans.at(candidate.compareOpIdx)
	let condId = minter.mint()
	origins.recordDerived(funcIndex, valueId: condId, sourceId: candidate.condId)
	module.appendOp(predBlock, op: StdOp.cmpImm(condId, lhs: incoming, imm: candidate.imm, pred: candidate.pred, operandType: candidate.operandType))

	let keptIsThen = candidate.keptTarget == candidate.thenBlockId
	let thenId = candidate.blockId if keptIsThen else candidate.droppedTarget
	let elseId = candidate.droppedTarget if keptIsThen else candidate.blockId
	try module.ops.set(predBlock.terminatorIndex(), value: StdOp.condBranch(condId, thenBlockId: thenId, elseBlockId: elseId)) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: ops.set OOB at terminator index {predBlock.terminatorIndex()}")

	var edges = BranchEdgeArray.create()
	edges.push(BranchEdge.create(candidate.blockId, argIds: argsToJoin))
	if droppedTakesArgs 'droppedTakesArgs'
		edges.push(BranchEdge.create(candidate.droppedTarget, argIds: substituteJoinArgs(argsToDropped, incoming: argsToJoin, index: index, argOwner: argOwner, argSlot: argSlot)))
	end 'droppedTakesArgs'
	predBlock.branchEdges = edges
end 'duplicateTestInto'

// C's edge args to the dropped target, as P must pass them: a block arg of C becomes the value P passes
// to that slot; anything else — including another join's block arg — is defined in a block dominating
// C, hence P, and passes through.
function substituteJoinArgs(argsToDropped ValueIdArray, incoming ValueIdArray, index CandidateIndex, argOwner ValueIdArray, argSlot ValueIdArray) returns ValueIdArray
	var substituted = ValueIdArray.create()

	for argId in argsToDropped 'eachArg'
		if not isOwnedByACandidate(argId, argOwner: argOwner) or candidateOwning(argId, argOwner: argOwner) != index 'definedAboveTheJoin'
			substituted.push(argId)
			continue
		end 'definedAboveTheJoin'

		let slot = try argSlot.get(argId) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: argSlot.get OOB at {argId}")
		substituted.push(try incoming.get(slot) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: the edge into the join passes {incoming.count()} arg(s) but slot {slot} is one of the join's block args"))
	end 'eachArg'

	return substituted
end 'substituteJoinArgs'

// Drop the tested slot of every rewritten join — the block arg and its slot in every incoming edge,
// through the one dropper both block-arg passes share. The count it answers must be exactly the
// rewrites: every tested arg lost its only reader with the compare, and no other arg is unmarked.
function dropTestedSlots(module StdModule, func IrFunction, candidates ThreadCandidateArray, applied ThreadedSiteCount)
	let refByBlockId = buildBlockIdIndex(module, func: func)
	let bound = blockArgIdBound(module, func: func)
	var kept = flagColumn(bound)

	for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'eachBlock'
		let block = module.getBlock(blockRef)
		for arg in block.blockArgs 'eachArg'
			setFlag(kept, v: arg.valueId)
		end 'eachArg'
	end 'eachBlock'

	for candidate in candidates 'eachCandidate'
		if candidate.admitted 'rewritten'
			try kept.set(candidate.testedArg, value: false) otherwise panic("threadConstantBranches: tested arg {candidate.testedArg} is outside the block-arg id space")
		end 'rewritten'
	end 'eachCandidate'

	let dropped = dropBlockArgs(module, func: func, refByBlockId: refByBlockId, kept: kept)
	if dropped != applied as ValueId 'countDisagrees'
		panic("threadConstantBranches: rewrote {applied} join(s) in '{String.from(func.name)}' but dropped {dropped} block arg(s) — a tested slot was not the only one unmarked, or was dropped twice")
	end 'countDisagrees'
end 'dropTestedSlots'
